				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/francis-willjam" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1394675); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1394675&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607892565" alt="Francis Willjam" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1394675)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/francis-willjam" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1394675); return false;" >Francis Willjam</a></span> <span class="odate time_1381413357 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Oct 2013 13:55</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1867983">
									

<p>Fixed a couple of minor errors but apart from that it seems good enough. I've got to say that the dialogue in the interview really took me out of the skip (when people use words like &quot;gal&quot; in what's meant to be a scientific document it always ruins immersion for me), but that's just personal preference.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Couple'a&nbsp;issues</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">chyeahchyeah</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>10m in length</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I really don't see the harm in making the outer/inner sizes make sense unless you have a particular reason not to.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1387 does not require nutrition, but recovers from injury quite slowly, with major injuries rendering the entity comatose for weeks.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The two statements in this sentence don't really seem to belong together imo, they're completely separate points.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>perform its primary effect</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Perform&quot; sounds a bit off to me. Perhaps 'initiate' or something similar.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is not possible to prevent instances of SCP-1387-1 from entering SCP-1387's interior</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems a bit far-fetched, it sounds as if all the foundation have tried is standing there saying &quot;oh no, don't go that way&quot; whereas they likely would have attempted to physically constrain the people. I'd suggest putting that attempting to prevent them from boarding causes them a large amount of distress.</p>
</div>
</div>
